@startuml
!theme plain
title D03 order status — transitions enforced by OrderStatus

[*] --> SCHEDULED : created (POST /orders)\nstatus must be null in the payload

SCHEDULED --> ON_ROUTE : completion callback\n(planned order)
SCHEDULED --> UNASSIGNED : completion callback\n(unplanned order)
SCHEDULED --> REJECTED : PATCH /orders/status
SCHEDULED --> UNASSIGNED : PATCH /orders/status

ON_ROUTE --> SERVICING : PATCH /orders/status
SERVICING --> COMPLETED : PATCH /orders/status
SERVICING --> REJECTED : PATCH /orders/status

COMPLETED --> SCHEDULED : PATCH /orders/status
UNASSIGNED --> SCHEDULED : PATCH /orders/status
REJECTED --> SCHEDULED : PATCH /orders/status

note right of SERVICING
  Allowed transitions come from OrderStatus.allowedTransitions:
  SCHEDULED   -> ON_ROUTE, UNASSIGNED, REJECTED
  ON_ROUTE    -> SERVICING
  SERVICING   -> COMPLETED, REJECTED
  COMPLETED   -> SCHEDULED
  UNASSIGNED  -> SCHEDULED
  REJECTED    -> SCHEDULED
end note

note bottom
  The callback path writes ON_ROUTE / UNASSIGNED directly on the entity and
  therefore does not consult this table; only PATCH /orders/status and the
  single-order transition service validate it.
  There is no CANCELLED state: a cancelled job leaves its orders untouched.
end note
@enduml
